# core.autocrlf is on, which would store the licence gate's Python with CRLF and
# check it out the same way. On the Linux runner that CI uses, a CRLF shebang
# makes the kernel look for an interpreter named `python3\r` — "bad
# interpreter", from a line that looks correct in every editor.
#
# Narrow on purpose. A blanket `* text=auto` here would renormalise every file
# in the repository in a commit that is supposed to be about something else;
# .editorconfig already carries the CRLF rule for everything but this.
*.py text eol=lf
